  "short_description": "W3C federated social networking standard \u2014 Mastodon, Lemmy, PeerTube, Pixelfed",
  "long_description": "ActivityPub 1.0 is the W3C standard protocol for federated social networking, enabling decentralized social applications to interoperate. The schema covers actor profiles (people, organizations, bots), content objects (posts, articles, notes, images), activity records (Create, Like, Announce/boost, Follow), and follower relationships \u2014 the complete ActivityStreams 2.0 vocabulary.",
  "when_to_use": "Use for federated social platforms, community discussion tools, or any social application that wants to be part of the Fediverse (Mastodon, Lemmy, PeerTube, Pixelfed ecosystem). ActivityPub implementations are growing rapidly following Twitter/X changes. Required for EU Digital Services Act compliance for large platforms needing interoperability APIs under consideration."
